packetq
------------------------------------------
packetq is a command line tool to run SQL queries directly on PCAP files, the
results can be outputted as JSON (default), formatted/compact CSV and XML. It
also contain a very simplistic web-server in order to inspect PCAP files
remotely. PacketQ was previously known as DNS2db but was renamed in 2011 when
it was rebuilt and could handle protocols other than DNS among other things.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libdnswire1-0.5.1-1bl1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libmaxminddb0-1.3.2-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  zlib0-1.3.2-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libdnswire-devel-0.5.1-1bl1
  libmaxminddb-devel-1.3.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2
  zlib-devel-1.3.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://www.dns-oarc.net/tools/packetq

Canonical download:
  https://www.dns-oarc.net/files/packetq/packetq-1.8.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack packetq-1.8.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./packetq-1.8.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/packetq-1.8.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/packetq-1.8.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(packetq)
